  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Continued rain through the weekend, with \nhighest amounts Downeast. The rainfall may provide some drought \nrelief.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA stationary front remains along the Maine coast early this\nmorning, with deep moisture advection moving northeast along the\nboundary and supporting ongoing rainfall throughout the Bangor\nand Downeast regions. A coastal low is projected to develop\nfurther south along this boundary, then move up along the New\nEngland coast through the day today, locally enhancing \nrainfall. Based on this synoptic and mesoscale pattern, enhanced\nrain amounts Downeast, particularly into the Washington County\ncoast, could exceed 2 inches by the time the storm system\nfinally exits to the east. Though this will by not means fix the\nongoing drought, this rainfall over a period of around 48 hours\ncould provide a little relief.\n\nAs the low pressure system collectively shifts eastward tonight\ninto the day on Sunday, rain will become more showery and spread\nnorthwards, encompassing the entire forecast area. Light rain\nshowers may last through Sunday morning before they themselves\nbegin to shift eastward with the departing low pressure.",
